+
+Step 27 leaves the interaction kernel unchanged and localizes the anomaly with:
+
+- `U''` jumps at every Hermite knot;
+- minimal distance/angle systems inside one cell versus knot crossing;
+- point-particle angle versus rigid-body virtual-site angle;
+- rotational finite differences against `torque_lab`;
+- full-system translational/rotational finite differences;
+- matched `no_ibi`, `bonds_only`, `angles_only`, and `full` scans with the WCA
+  topology preserved;
+- knot-crossing versus per-step `|Delta E|` correlation;
+- translational/rotational kinetic plus bonded/non-bonded energy decomposition;
+- link-cell versus all-pairs N-square traversal;
+- forward / reverse-velocity / forward time reversibility.
+
+The main artifact is
+`conservative_ibi_energy_localization/localization_report.json`. If an
+inside-cell micro-system recovers `sigma_E ~ dt^2` while the corresponding
+knot-crossing system does not, knot regularity is strongly implicated. If the
+point-angle case passes but the rigid-angle case fails, investigate virtual-site
+force/torque back-transfer and rotational integration. If `no_ibi` also fails,
+do not blame the spline representation.
+
+Until a reproducible `sigma_E ~ dt^2` failure is localized, the composite step-26
+PASS must not be interpreted as explaining or closing that specific energy-
+scaling anomaly.
 
